  "behavior": "Cache only class attributes of 64\u20138192 bytes with at most 128 token hashes. Tag, ID and attribute-name hashing remains live. Each style computer owns 128 slots keyed by full live node/document identities, attribute epoch, class-source identity/length and quirks. Address bits above alignment select slots. The first admitted node keeps its slot within an epoch, avoiding traversal churn; stale epochs and the same node can replace contents. Foreign documents bypass caching. Vectors contain scalar hashes only, are explicitly typed before append, and reuse their reservation.",
  "bounded_payload": "At most 128 slots times 128 u32 hashes: 65,536 scalar payload bytes. Descriptors, vector headers and allocator storage are additional. Allocation follows the saved-visit caller\u2019s document-retained scope. Warm hit loops preserve caller-arena usage and payload backing.",
  "control": "VOX_RETAIN_ANCESTOR_HASH_RECOMPUTE=1; same final class-token loop with memo disabled, existing saved ancestor-pop hashes enabled in both variants. Common dispatch differs from older release code.",
